---
const principles = [
  { title: 'Open by default', text: 'Papers, code, and data are released together.' },
  { title: 'Reproducible', text: 'Every claim ships with the setup needed to rerun it.' },
  { title: 'Evidence first', text: 'We report variance, failures, and negative results.' },
];
---

<section id="about" class="scroll-mt-28 py-24 md:py-32 border-t border-white/[0.06]">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8 lg:gap-12">
    <div class="lg:col-span-3">
      <p class="section-label lg:sticky lg:top-28">01 — About</p>
    </div>

    <div class="lg:col-span-9">
      <p data-reveal class="text-2xl sm:text-4xl font-light leading-snug tracking-tight text-slate-200">
        <em class="not-italic text-celestial font-normal">Zetesis</em> comes from the Greek
        <span class="text-white font-normal">ζήτησις</span>: the act of searching, questioning, and investigating.
        We think the most capable AI systems will be the ones that do the same.
      </p>

      <div data-reveal class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 text-slate-400 leading-relaxed font-light" style="--reveal-delay: 120ms;">
        <p>
          Today's models answer well but rarely ask. We study how AI systems can form their own questions, split them across cooperating agents, gather evidence, and revise what they believe. Our work sits between machine learning research and systems engineering.
        </p>
        <p>
          We are a small, independent collective of researchers and engineers. We keep our methods simple, our experiments reproducible, and our results public, so that others can check them, build on them, or prove them wrong.
        </p>
      </div>

      <dl data-reveal class="mt-16 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 border-t border-white/[0.08]" style="--reveal-delay: 240ms;">
        {principles.map((p) => (
          <div class="pt-6 pb-2 sm:pr-6">
            <dt class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-white mb-2">{p.title}</dt>
            <dd class="text-sm text-slate-400 font-light">{p.text}</dd>
          </div>
        ))}
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
